   "cat": "structure",
   "label": "Emphatic Climax",
   "quote": "ipse potius amator advolavi tibi",
   "trans": "I, your lover, have flown to you myself instead",
   "body": "The speech lands on a proud, wounded declaration: <em>ipse ... amator ... advolavi tibi</em> — \"I myself, your lover, flew to you instead\". The emphatic <em>ipse</em> and first-person verb set Cupid’s devotion against his mother’s command.",
   "exam": "<strong>In an exam:</strong> \"The emphatic <em>ipse ... amator advolavi tibi</em> is the climax of Cupid’s reproach: the intensive pronoun and first-person verb stress that he, the god himself, chose Psyche against Venus’s orders — making her betrayal sting all the more.\"",
   "line": ""
  },
